# N3 example: check-unsafe.
# Companion to check-unsafe.eye/.srl: like the source warning, ?someone
# is deliberately not bound by the antecedent.
#
# A third distinct behavior for the same unsafe pattern: SRL statically
# rejects the rule set with an "unbound head variable" error; Eyelang (by
# design, matching its own upstream reference behavior) runs it and
# leaks the literal unbound variable into the answer; N3, confirmed by
# testing, silently derives nothing at all -- no error, no leaked
# variable, and no :Seen fact for any binding of ?someone.

@prefix : <https://eyereasoner.github.io/eyepl/examples/check-unsafe#>.

:alice :knows :bob.

{:alice :knows :bob} => {?someone a :Seen}.
